Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 11:20:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Install into the vbcc toolchain and document the host build

make -f Makefile-host install lays ACE out the way the other components of
~/Dev/amiga are laid out: binaries flat in bin/, driver config in
config/ace68k, everything else as an SDK under sdk/ACE keeping its own
directory names.  submods/ is installed too, because sources reach their
objects through the ace: assign and bas maps that onto ACE_HOME.

Changes inside ~/Dev/amiga are not versioned, so the previous contents of
setenv_*.sh, CROSSCOMPILE.md and makefiles/ were copied to
~/Dev/amiga/.backup-before-ace first:

  setenv_{mac,lin,win}.sh   ACE_HOME/ACE_LIB/ACE_INC/ACE_BMAPS
  makefiles/Makefile.*      BAS, MV and the ACE_* paths; the AmigaOS
                            variant uses the assigns and `rename`
  makefiles/Makefile.rules  BASIC_SOURCES alongside C_SOURCES and
                            ASM_SOURCES, with a %.o: %.b rule (bas -m
                            writes next to the source, so it is moved)
  CROSSCOMPILE.md           new section 6 on ACE, incl. the first-dot
                            filename trap when calling ace directly

README.md gains a Host Installation section; AGENTS.md gains a section
telling future agents to iterate with Makefile-host instead of the
emulator, and to run amiga-check alongside it - the two builds disagree
about what LONG is, which is exactly what catches format bugs.

Verified from a clean environment with nothing but setenv_mac.sh sourced:
all 223 non-error cases build to AmigaOS executables, all 28 errors/ cases
are rejected, a LIBRARY call still resolves through the bmaps to
jsr -96(a6), and the Makefile template compiles a .b module via
BASIC_SOURCES.

