+### Host Cross-Compiler — use this to iterate
+
+`Makefile-host` builds `ace`, `yap` and `bas` as native host binaries, so the
+whole pipeline runs on macOS/Linux/Windows without the emulator. This is by
+far the fastest way to test compiler changes.
+
+```bash
+cd src/make
+export VBCC=~/Dev/amiga        # supplies vasmm68k_mot and vlink
+make -f Makefile-host          # -> bin/host/<platform>/{ace,yap,bas}
+make -f Makefile-host amiga-check   # cross-build for m68k: does the
+                                    # AmigaOS code path still compile?
+make -f Makefile-host install  # install into $VBCC
+```
+
+**After any change to `src/ace/c/`, run BOTH** `make -f Makefile-host` and
+`make -f Makefile-host amiga-check`. The host build has `-Werror=format`
+because `LONG` is exactly 32 bits there; the amiga-check build catches the
+mirror-image mistake, since `LONG` is `long` under vbcc. Format conversions
+must therefore carry explicit C-type casts — `(long)` with `%ld`,
+`(unsigned long)` with `%lx` — or one of the two compilers will complain.
+
+Host-specific code sits behind `ACE_HOST`:
+- `src/ace/c/hostcompat.h` — exact-width Amiga base types. `LONG` must stay
+  32-bit (`FLOAT_BITS`) and `SHORT` 16-bit (`.bmap` LVO sign extension).
+- `src/ace/c/break.c` — Ctrl-C handling. Separate from `lex.c` because
+  `acedef.h` declares ACE's own `kill()`, which collides with POSIX `kill()`.
+
+`ACE_BMAPS`, `ACE_INC` and `ACE_HOME` override the `ACEbmaps:`,
+`ACEinclude:` and `ACE:` assigns; unset, the assign names are used, so the
+Amiga behaviour is unchanged.
+
+Verification without an Amiga:
+```bash
+utils/yap/tests/run_tests.sh                    # yap vs the BASIC original
+verify/scripts/compare-host-vs-amiga.sh         # emitted .s, host vs m68k
+```
+The second needs `vamos` (`pip install amitools 'machine68k<0.4'`).
+
